	(text "Set the external step-down module to 5.0 V BEFORE connecting it. If its preset fails, D3 conducts and F2 trips.\nP6KE22A clamps load-dump spikes (Vc ~31 V) below the 40 V limit of LM2596 modules. D1 blocks reverse polarity."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 22.86 106.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c4fc4e67-5954-52e7-987d-901be074daa9")
	)
	(text "Coil primary pulses are 200-400 V (more with the spark plug disconnected).\nNever run the engine with the plug cap off. HV nets (RPM_IN..RPM_C) keep 2.5 mm clearance on the PCB.\nFirmware: PA6 as TIM3_CH1 input capture WITH internal pull-up; ignore pulses closer than ~2 ms (ignition ringing)."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 22.86 175.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2acc474b-bdc7-5686-8011-08a2a71ca878")
	)
	(text "Pin numbers follow the Blue Pill headers: 1-20 = VB..GND row, 21-40 = 3.3/GND/5V..B12 row.\nPin 21 (3.3) is tied to pin 18 inside the module. Check the silkscreen labels against the module before soldering.\nPA0 (button) and PA6 (RPM) need the internal pull-up enabled in firmware."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 210.82 238.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2a640011-303e-5233-92dd-dde0b79cb188")
	)
